   "text": "As of May 2026, the U.S. median sale price stood at $449,846, up 2.2% year over year, while inventory fell 9.0% to 1,460,440 listings. Homes are taking a median of 42 days to sell, two days longer than a year ago, and the share of listings with price drops rose to 20.0%, up 1.4pp. Among the top alerts, 22 metros saw monthly payments rise at least 10% year over year, and 4 metros recorded inventory declines of 24% year over year. The 30-year mortgage rate is 7.03%, up 0.08pp from a week earlier and above the 6.3% level of a year ago. Nationally, 28 of the 50 tracked metros now have more price cuts than a year ago, and the overall market temperature reads Balanced with a score of 59.",
